IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wpa-types`
IMPORT `wpa-deductions`

-- Wages Protection Act 1983 — GOAL 2: WERE THE WAGES PAID IN A LAWFUL
-- MANNER?
--
--   "Were the wages paid in money, or in another manner the Act allows —
--    a specified cheque from the Crown or a local authority, a postal order,
--    money order, specified cheque or bank lodgement with the worker's
--    written consent or request, or a postal order, money order or
--    specified cheque to an absent worker?"
--
-- Source: ../source/WPA1983.txt — ss 2, 7, 8, 9, 10, 15, 16, 17.

§ `Goal 2 — the manner of payment`

-- s 9(1)-(2): the worker's written consent or request, not withdrawn by the
-- s 9(2) day.
@ref s 9
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker's consent or request to the manner of payment covers` p IF
        p's `the worker's written consent or request to be paid this way`
    AND `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (p's `paid on`) `, notice` (p's `notice withdrawing the consent or request`)

-- s 7 "Subject to sections 8 to 10, an employer shall pay the wages of every
-- worker in money only."
-- s 8 "The Crown, or a local authority, may pay to a worker by specified
-- cheque".
-- s 9(1) with the worker's written consent or request, "by postal order,
-- money order, specified cheque, or lodgement at a financial institution to
-- the credit of an account standing in the name of that worker or in the name
-- of that worker and some other person or persons jointly".
-- s 10 a worker "absent from the proper or usual place for their payment"
-- may be paid "by postal order, money order, or specified cheque".
-- s 15 (other Acts), s 16 (collective agreements and orders) and s 17 (a
-- bearer-cheque contract made before 17 November 1964) are inputs.
@ref ss 7, 8, 9, 10, 15, 16, 17
@export Whether wages were paid in a manner the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ) allows: in money (s 7); by specified cheque from the Crown or a local authority (s 8); by postal order, money order, specified cheque or lodgement to an account in the worker's name (alone or jointly) with the worker's written consent or request, not withdrawn (s 9); by postal order, money order or specified cheque to a worker absent from the usual place of payment (s 10); or as another Act, a collective agreement, an order or a pre-1964 contract allows (ss 15-17). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc How the wages were paid, when, by whom (the Crown or a local authority?), whether the worker consented or asked in writing (and any withdrawal), whether the worker was absent from the usual place of payment, and any ss 15-17 authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wages were paid in a lawful manner` p IF
        p's `permitted by another Act, a collective agreement or an order (ss 15, 16)`
    OR  p's `under a contract for payment by bearer cheque made before 17 November 1964`
    OR  CONSIDER p's `manner`
        WHEN `money` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a specified cheque (payable to, or to the order of, the worker)` THEN
                p's `the employer is the Crown or a local authority`
             OR `the worker's consent or request to the manner of payment covers` p
             OR p's `the worker was absent from the proper or usual place of payment`
        WHEN `a postal order` THEN
                `the worker's consent or request to the manner of payment covers` p
             OR p's `the worker was absent from the proper or usual place of payment`
        WHEN `a money order` THEN
                `the worker's consent or request to the manner of payment covers` p
             OR p's `the worker was absent from the proper or usual place of payment`
        WHEN `lodgement at a financial institution` `in the worker's name` THEN
                `in the worker's name`
            AND `the worker's consent or request to the manner of payment covers` p
        WHEN `some other manner` THEN FALSE
